</div>

## SECTION 2 — LESSON IDENTIFICATION TABLE
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color:#1a5276;">Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color:#1a5276;">Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color:#1a5276;">Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color:#1a5276;">Scenario:</b> Managing Stress in Changing Times</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color:#1a5276;">Theme:</b> Breathing to Relax</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color:#1a5276;">Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b style="color:#1a5276;">Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color:#1a5276;">Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write reviews on general products or services. Interactive: Revise classmates' essays on general topics.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color:#1a5276;">Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a comparative review of two wellness strategies, integrating real-life examples from local surroundings or meditation apps (e.g., "The daily meditation app I downloaded is great, but hiking in the rainforest provides a unique sensory experience.")
            Can edit classmates' essays on wellness practices, suggesting improvements and clarifying points (e.g., "Consider explaining how breathing exercises reduce stress.")
            Can revise essays by adding suggestions of stress management techniques (e.g., "You should include how meditation helps you focus.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

## SECTION 3 — AOA STAGES TABLE
<h2 style="color:#1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color:#1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%; color:#1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color:#1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color:#1a5276; margin-top:0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays images of people practicing different relaxation techniques (e.g., deep breathing, listening to soothing music, forest bathing). Students individually write down 2-3 sentences describing which technique looks most appealing and why it might be beneficial for managing stress. They should use target vocabulary like 'relaxation,' 'mindfulness,' 'soothing,' and 'reduce stress'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to express advice and suggestions for stress management in writing, focusing on gerunds and modals. For example, "<i>Practicing mindfulness</i> helps to <i>improve</i> focus." or "You <i>should try spending</i> 10 minutes meditating in a quiet spot." The teacher highlights the use of gerunds after prepositions or as subjects, and modals for advice. The teacher also reads aloud the model sentences, emphasizing the long vowel sound /uː/ in 'soothing' and 'smooth' and the reduced vowels in 'mindfulness' and 'beneficial' to reinforce accurate reading and writing of these words.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What type of word do we use after a preposition like 'for' when we are describing an activity? (e.g., 'good for...')" (Expected answer: A gerund / -ing form)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What modal verb can we use to give strong advice about stress management techniques?" (Expected answer: 'should' or 'must')</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(8-10 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color:#1a5276; margin-top:0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Managing Stress in Changing Times")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher presents a short, authentic blog post excerpt (approx. 150-180 words) titled "Two Pathways to Inner Peace: A Comparative Review." The text compares two wellness strategies (e.g., "meditation apps" vs. "forest bathing"), integrating examples from local surroundings if possible. It explicitly uses gerunds (e.g., "<i>Practicing</i> deep breathing...", "<i>Listening</i> to music..."), modals for advice (e.g., "You <i>should try</i>...", "People <i>could benefit</i> from..."), and present continuous for trends (e.g., "Many people <i>are seeking</i> new ways...", "Wellness apps <i>are becoming</i> popular..."). The text also includes key vocabulary such as 'breathing,' 'relaxation,' 'mindfulness,' 'meditation,' 'wellness,' 'techniques,' 'stress,' 'focus,' 'beneficial,' and 'soothing.'</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Writing: Productive: Write reviews on general products or services.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the blog post silently and then complete the following writing tasks:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question:</b> Write a sentence summarizing the main purpose of the blog post.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Students write down which wellness strategy (meditation app or forest bathing) is associated with the following benefits/features, quoting directly from the text where possible:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Offers 'unique sensory experience.'</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Provides 'guided practices.'</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is 'becoming a popular trend.'</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(10-12 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color:#1a5276; margin-top:0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Writing)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing sentences using Gerunds, Modals for advice, and Present continuous for trends, along with target vocabulary (breathing, relaxation, mindfulness, meditation, stress, wellness, techniques, practices, mind, body, balance, relief, habits, quiet spot, focus, beneficial, calming, effective, peaceful).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Transformation:</b> Students are given sentences and instructed to rewrite them using a gerund as the subject or after a preposition, or using a modal for advice.
                        <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"To meditate daily helps with focus." (Rewrite using a gerund: "<i>Meditating</i> daily helps with focus.")</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"It is advisable to try deep breathing." (Rewrite using a modal: "You <i>should try deep breathing</i>.")</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Many people find new ways to reduce stress." (Rewrite using present continuous: "Many people <i>are finding</i> new ways to reduce stress.")</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Paragraph Completion:</b> Students complete a short paragraph (3-4 sentences) describing a chosen wellness practice. They are provided with sentence starters and a bank of target vocabulary (e.g., 'relax,' 'improve,' 'mindfulness,' 'stress-free,' 'beneficial') and must correctly use gerunds and modals.
                        <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"<i>Listening</i> to music is a great way to ______ (relax). You ______ (should/could) try it for <i>gaining</i> better focus. This practice is ______ (beneficial) for everyone."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Check & Revision:</b> In pairs, students exchange their completed paragraphs from the previous activity. They read each other's work and politely write down one suggestion for improvement related to grammar (gerunds/modals) or vocabulary use, and one positive comment. They use phrases like "You <i>could try</i> adding..." or "I suggest <i>revising</i> the part about..." This activity reinforces sociolinguistic and pragmatic functions.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(10-12 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color:#1a5276; margin-top:0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Managing Stress in Changing Times")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual Written Product – A Comparative Review.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b> Students will write a comparative review (120-150 words) of two wellness strategies they are familiar with, or have researched, to manage stress. The review should include:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">An introduction to the two strategies.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A description of each, including their benefits.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A comparison/contrast, using real-life examples from local surroundings (e.g., "<i>Hiking</i> in Omar Park provides a unique sensory experience") or apps.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A recommendation for who might benefit from each, using modals for advice.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A concluding statement.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students are encouraged to use a variety of gerunds, modals for advice, present continuous for trends, and the target vocabulary (e.g., 'breathing,' 'relaxation,' 'mindfulness,' 'meditation,' 'wellness-focused,' 'effective,' 'soothing,' 'beneficial,' 'reduce,' 'improve,' 'focus,' 'manage'). The teacher reminds students to structure their review logically with clear paragraphs.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(12-15 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color:#1a5276; margin-top:0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Peer Assessment with a Checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students exchange their comparative reviews with a partner. Each student reads their partner's review and uses a provided checklist to assess it. After completing the checklist, they write 2-3 specific suggestions for improvement directly on the review, focusing on clarity, grammar, vocabulary, and organization. For instance, "<i>Consider explaining</i> how breathing exercises reduce stress" or "You <i>should include</i> how meditation helps you focus." They also highlight one sentence that effectively uses a gerund or modal.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Checklist items):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clear introduction and conclusion? (Clarity)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses appropriate target vocabulary? (Vocabulary use)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of gerunds? (Grammar accuracy)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of modals for advice? (Grammar accuracy)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Includes real-life examples? (Content relevance)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Suggestions for improvement are polite and clear? (Sociolinguistic/Pragmatic)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students reflect on their own writing process and their partner's feedback by answering these prompts:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I learned about writing comparative reviews today is..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I feel confident/less confident using gerunds and modals in my writing because..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(5-7 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color:#1a5276; margin-top:0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h4>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of the writing process (planning, drafting, revising) did I find most challenging today, and why?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I apply the feedback I received to improve my next piece of writing about wellness?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The modeling and practice activities for writing gerunds and modals were effective because students demonstrated clear understanding in their reviews and peer feedback. The use of specific local examples helped make the content relevant."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Some students struggled with the organization of their comparative reviews. For the next writing task, I will provide a more structured outline or a clear template to guide their composition more effectively. More targeted practice on sentence combining might also be beneficial."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This writing lesson has equipped students with the ability to describe and compare wellness strategies using specific grammatical structures and vocabulary. In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will use this written output as a basis to summarize and explain these wellness practices to a broader audience, possibly creating a multimedia presentation or an informational brochure. They will need to consolidate their written ideas and adapt them for a different purpose and audience.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(5 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>